# Nowo.tech kits and legal reminders

When implementing product features in this repo, **prefer official `nowo-tech/*` Symfony bundles** instead of reinventing auth, users, audit fields, cookies, or legal UX.

## Prefer these kits (do not hand-roll equivalents)

| Need | Package | Notes |
|------|---------|--------|
| Login / registration / password reset UI | `nowo-tech/auth-kit-bundle` | Configurable flows, Twig overrides, i18n |
| User enable/disable, last activity, online | `nowo-tech/user-kit-bundle` | Account lifecycle on top of Security |
| createdAt/updatedAt + blame fields | `nowo-tech/audit-kit-bundle` | Opt-in Doctrine timestamps/blame |
| Cookie / GDPR consent modal | `nowo-tech/cookie-consent-bundle` | ≥1.9: link `nowo-cookie-consent.css` + `data-nowo-cookie-consent-css` (CSP); categories + optional consent logging |
| Login throttling | `nowo-tech/login-throttle-bundle` | Wraps Symfony `login_throttling` |
| Password policy / strength / toggle | `nowo-tech/password-*-bundle` | Prefer kits over custom validators/UI |
| Breadcrumb trails (DB + Twig) | `nowo-tech/breadcrumb-kit-bundle` | Route matching, i18n, optional admin CRUD |
| Dashboard menus (DB + Twig/API) | `nowo-tech/dashboard-menu-bundle` | Tree menus, i18n, permissions, admin CRUD |
| Admin UI macros / `nowo-ui-*` CSS / modals | `nowo-tech/ui-kit-bundle` | Host: `css_framework: tailwind`, `icon_set: ux_icon`; remap tokens under `.kit-admin`; ≥1.8 Stimulus peers (clipboard/confirm/toast/tabs/page-loader) |
| Symfony forms (options merge, i18n conventions) | `nowo-tech/form-kit-bundle` | Prefer over hand-rolled form themes / labels; kit profiles for AuthKit/admin; ≥2.4 CSRF-only + GET filter factories (`090` / `101`) |
| Phone / E.164 country-prefix inputs | `nowo-tech/phone-input-bundle` | Account → Profile (`100`); ≥1.3 CSP-safe kit picker — do not hand-roll dial codes or host Twig/JS forks. Thin `_phone_input.scss` theme bridge is allowed (Bootstrap tokens → Beacon `--color-*`) |
| Progressive Web App (manifest, SW, install) | `nowo-tech/pwa-bundle` | Prefer over hand-rolled service workers. Do **not** fork `pwa/install_links.html.twig` (vendor + host SCSS BEM + Preferences hint) |
| Dual locale public paths (`/foo` + `/{locale}/foo`) | `nowo-tech/routing-kit-bundle` | `#[Routable]` + panel `/_routing/`; AuthKit/SiteBackup keep their own locale config |
| HTTP request/response audit log + admin | `nowo-tech/http-log-bundle` | Admin `/admin/http-log`; async Messenger persist; host layout `kit/http_log_admin_layout.html.twig` |
| Client SDK for this Beacon server | `nowo-tech/beacon-bundle` | DSN (`BEACON_DSN`) with host/port; Envelope ingest. Also installed **in this server** for dogfooding when `BEACON_DSN` is set. |
| Field encryption | `nowo-tech/doctrine-encrypt-bundle` | Halite; API secrets + webhook URLs + Mailer DSN |
| Twig debug overlay | `nowo-tech/twig-inspector-bundle` | Already used in `require-dev` |
| FrankenPHP hot reload (dev client) | `nowo-tech/hot-reload-bundle` | ≥**1.3.2**: auto-inject + CSP nonce/augment + `@NowoHotReloadBundle` WDT panel + Twig Extra; prefer over hand-rolled Vite/Twig Idiomorph wiring |

Packagist vendor: https://packagist.org/packages/nowo-tech/

## Before inventing Identity/Security UI

1. Ask whether `auth-kit-bundle` + `user-kit-bundle` cover the need.
2. Prefer integrating those bundles (Flex recipes, template overrides) over growing `src/Identity` with bespoke login/register CRUD.
3. Use `audit-kit-bundle` for entity timestamps/blame instead of copying trait logic.

## Legal notice / privacy / terms (ALWAYS remind)

When touching public UI, marketing pages, cookies, analytics, contact forms, or self-hosted SaaS surfaces, **remind the user** and propose:

- Legal notice / privacy / terms pages as English UI copy (`lang="en"`), with room for operator-specific text.
- Cookie consent via `nowo-tech/cookie-consent-bundle` when any non-essential cookie or third-party script appears (Vite analytics, embeds, etc.).
- GDPR-oriented data handling (`anonymize-bundle`, encrypt-bundle) when storing personal data beyond auth essentials.

Do **not** silently ship tracking or optional cookies without consent UX.

## Current project status (honest baseline)

Identity already uses **AuthKit** for login/registration (`registration_mode: first_user_only`), plus UserKit / AuditKit / password kits for account lifecycle. Phase 6 `037-authkit-identity-migration` is **kit polish** (area nav, social links, security activity) — **not** a greenfield AuthKit migration; see `specs/037-authkit-identity-migration/`. Do not reintroduce a custom `SecurityController`.

## Agent behaviour

- If the user asks for login, registration, memberships, audit columns, forms, or legal/cookie UX → **mention the matching nowo-tech package first**, then implement with it unless they explicitly refuse.
- Keep docs/PHPDoc/UI strings in English (see `english-docs-and-phpdoc` rule).
